{
    "background_story": "Mark was a free-spirited traveler with a knack for finding himself in the most unexpected adventures. His life was a series of episodic encounters, each one a self-contained story waiting to be told. One day, he'd be sipping coffee with a nomadic tribe in the Sahara; the next, he'd be island-hopping in Greece, searching for the perfect souvlaki. Mark's travels were marked by chance meetings and spontaneous decisions, leading him to work as a fisherman in Alaska, a bartender in Tokyo, and even a extra in a Bollywood film. His friends and family would often receive postcards from exotic locations, each one a brief glimpse into Mark's latest escapade. Though his life was fragmented into a series of disconnected episodes, Mark wouldn't have had it any other way \u2013 for him, the journey was the destination.",
